Hi Gabriela,

This problem has been solved in the developing version of dartR, you can install this version by using:

# library required to install from github
library(devtools)
# installing developing version of dartR
install_github("green-striped-gecko/dartR@dev")

# if you are working with R-studio restart your session with menu Session -> Restart R

library(dartR)

To make things easier, check that the field in which your sex information is contained is in your_gl$other$ind.metrics$sex.
Also, it would be a good idea to explore different threshold values for this function, I think the default value is a bit stringent.
Then you can try:

res <- gl.report.sexlinked(platypus.gl <http://platypus.gl>, t.het = 0.2, t.hom = 0.2)

Please let us know whether this worked for you.

Cheers,
Luis

